From: Erik Dubois <erik.dubois@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Kiro: replaces=('python-pywal')

provides/conflicts alone never swaps an installed python-pywal on
pacman -Syu; replaces does. Installed Kiro systems still on the archived
pywal 3.3 move to pywal16 on their next update.

Local Kiro delta, not upstream AUR.
---
diff --git a/PKGBUILD b/PKGBUILD
index 6c86a97..dd60a2e 100644
--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ conflicts=(
   'pywal'
   'python-pywal'
 )
+replaces=('python-pywal')
 source=("${_archive_name}::${url}/archive/refs/tags/${pkgver}.tar.gz")
 sha256sums=('cd3e4588c453b844dd222d861b52b7a7c88a3396b3e104300ef1db27b9492b1d')
 
